    "raw": "To determine the number of pets at the shelter after one month, we need to calculate the number of pets adopted and then add the new pets taken in.\n\n1. **Initial number of pets:**\n   - Dogs: 30\n   - Cats: 28\n   - Lizards: 20\n\n2. **Adoptions:**\n   - Dogs: 50% of 30 = 0.50 * 30 = 15 dogs adopted\n   - Cats: 25% of 28 = 0.25 * 28 = 7 cats adopted\n   - Lizards: 20% of 20 = 0.20 * 20 = 4 lizards adopted\n\n3. **Remaining pets after adoptions:**\n   - Dogs: 30 - 15 = 15\n   - Cats: 28 - 7 = 21\n   - Lizards: 20 - 4 = 16\n\n4. **New pets taken in:**\n   - The shelter takes in 13 new pets each month.\n\n5. **Total number of pets after one month:**\n   - Total pets = Remaining dogs + Remaining cats + Remaining lizards + New pets\n   - Total pets = 15 + 21 + 16 + 13 = 65\n\nThe number of pets at the shelter after one month is 65.\n\nFINAL: 65",
